    answer:
      'A Florida quitclaim deed requires two witnesses in addition to a notary public, under Fla. Stat. § 689.01. The grantor must sign the deed in the presence of two subscribing witnesses. Both witnesses must sign the deed itself. A deed signed before only one witness is defective under Florida law, even if a notary is present. This is the most common error in generic, nationally-distributed deed templates used for Florida property.',
