    answer:
      "Yes, if the property is the grantor's homestead. Under the Florida Constitution (art. X, § 4), homestead property cannot be conveyed without the joinder of the owner's spouse, even if the spouse's name does not appear on the title. This applies to the grantor's primary residence. If the property is not homestead — for example, an investment property or rental the grantor does not occupy as their primary home — spousal joinder is not required by the homestead provision.",
