    question: 'Does a quitclaim deed remove me from the mortgage in Florida?',
    answer:
      'No. A quitclaim deed transfers property title only — not mortgage liability. If your name is on the mortgage, you remain liable for the debt even after your name is removed from the deed. Removal from the mortgage requires a lender refinance or formal release, not a deed. This is especially important in Florida divorce situations: a decree ordering one spouse to take the property does not automatically remove the other spouse from the mortgage.',
